# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-7 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-7 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-7 throughout.
# H7: hand the cards back to production. This is the LAST job of the window and it runs even when a stop job (B7, M7 or SR7) halted the
# window and after a stall or a hang, which are expected to be able to leave all four cards hung with production down: the status of
# every board and the all-four reset. The driver then runs, outside this job file, the platform's fabric re-measure, the :latest retag
# in the rig daemon's local store, and placement through the admin API (which needs the user's go-ahead and an admin token); then
# /v1/models and one chat on the placed production endpoint.
# What to place: tp4-serve-7 (the verified winning recipe: c2-packed-tp4 with the verify audits off and the sampler in the verify trace)
# ONLY if B7, M7 and SR7 all passed. If any of them failed or was skipped, re-place the image that was in production before this window
# (audits on), never tp4-serve-7. NEVER place a gate arm in either case: not c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace, not any gate-only profile.
# Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the fabric re-measure passes, the endpoint answers /v1/models with
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt and a chat completes, and the engine log shows profile c2-packed-tp4 with, for tp4-serve-7, the audits off and
# QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE=1 (for the previous image, the audits on). If the reset does not heal a board after a stall,
# production stays down until it does.
# Duration (estimate): 15 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (it is the last job).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-7
